    {
      "number": 11,
      "id": "PR_kwDOU6xPE88AAAABKm4C8g",
      "title": "Encode TIMESTAMP_MAPPING integers the same way on every MOQT version",
      "url": "https://github.com/afrind/draft-frindell-moq-timestamp/pull/11",
      "state": "MERGED",
      "author": "gmarzot",
      "authorAssociation": "CONTRIBUTOR",
      "assignees": [],
      "labels": [],
      "body": "Relays forward TIMESTAMP_MAPPING unchanged. When its integers followed the session's varint encoding, a relay bridging a draft-18 publisher to a draft-16 subscriber corrupted it. We saw this in interop through moqx: CMAF video was rejected as malformed, and audio timing decoded silently to wrong values.\n\nAs Alan suggested, this notes where the encoding was introduced, and that the mapping's integers aren't re-encoded over a draft-16 or earlier session.\n",
      "createdAt": "2026-10-25T17:06:48Z",
      "updatedAt": "2026-10-31T20:33:55Z",
      "baseRepository": "afrind/draft-frindell-moq-timestamp",
      "baseRefName": "main",
      "baseRefOid": "9f67ec744f103d2ce8afb6e07e47430f155376e4",
      "headRepository": "gmarzot/draft-frindell-moq-timestamp",
      "headRefName": "mapping-vi64",
      "headRefOid": "516ef16fa608b88ac161f9482c17840e8e28ca15",
      "closedAt": "2026-10-31T20:33:55Z",
      "mergedAt": "2026-10-31T20:33:55Z",
      "mergedBy": "afrind",
      "mergeCommit": {
        "oid": "6553526eb16fc21d0972d28e80649d4b5c88f019"
      },
      "comments": [],
      "reviews": [
        {
          "id": "PRR_kwDOU6xPE88AAAABUG2fyg",
          "commit": {
            "abbreviatedOid": "deb6af3"
          },
          "author": "afrind",
          "authorAssociation": "OWNER",
          "state": "COMMENTED",
          "body": "",
          "createdAt": "2026-10-25T17:22:03Z",
          "updatedAt": "2026-10-25T17:22:53Z",
          "comments": [
            {
              "originalPosition": 5,
              "body": "I'd try to say more with less.  You can add the \"introduced in draft-17?\" note to the parenthetical aside in the first sentence, then a single sentence that says passing this property over a draft-16 or earlier session does not re-encode the varints.\r\n\r\nLength prefixed is irrelevant.",
              "createdAt": "2026-10-25T17:22:03Z",
              "updatedAt": "2026-10-25T17:22:53Z"
            },
            {
              "originalPosition": 20,
              "body": "not sure we need this backref?  Seems unambiguous.",
              "createdAt": "2026-10-25T17:22:43Z",
              "updatedAt": "2026-10-25T17:22:53Z"
            },
            {
              "originalPosition": 31,
              "body": "Same",
              "createdAt": "2026-10-25T17:22:49Z",
              "updatedAt": "2026-10-25T17:22:53Z"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "PRR_kwDOU6xPE88AAAABUG5bYQ",
          "commit": {
            "abbreviatedOid": "516ef16"
          },
          "author": "gmarzot",
          "authorAssociation": "CONTRIBUTOR",
          "state": "COMMENTED",
          "body": "",
          "createdAt": "2026-10-25T17:37:31Z",
          "updatedAt": "2026-10-25T17:37:31Z",
          "comments": [
            {
              "originalPosition": 5,
              "body": "Done: two sentences, and both back-refs dropped. I named TIMESTAMP_MAPPING rather than all Property values, because on a draft-16 session a varint-valued property is framed by the session's own Key-Value-Pair encoding, so only the mapping's integers stay as they are.",
              "createdAt": "2026-10-25T17:37:31Z",
              "updatedAt": "2026-10-25T17:37:31Z"
            }
          ]
        },
