    {
      "number": 16,
      "id": "PR_kwDOU6xPE88AAAABL2d7LA",
      "title": "Allow TIMESTAMP_ORIGIN on POSIX-time Tracks",
      "url": "https://github.com/afrind/draft-frindell-moq-timestamp/pull/16",
      "state": "MERGED",
      "author": "afrind",
      "authorAssociation": "OWNER",
      "assignees": [],
      "labels": [],
      "body": "Since #4, omitting CLOCK_ID places a Track on POSIX time, so the rule that TIMESTAMP_ORIGIN requires CLOCK_ID left wall-clock Tracks unable to use an origin and forced every Object to carry a full epoch timestamp. Drop the rule, and update Security Considerations, which still assumed omitting CLOCK_ID hid the timeline's placement.\n\nFixes #13",
      "createdAt": "2026-10-30T19:57:22Z",
      "updatedAt": "2026-10-31T12:57:18Z",
      "baseRepository": "afrind/draft-frindell-moq-timestamp",
      "baseRefName": "main",
      "baseRefOid": "9f67ec744f103d2ce8afb6e07e47430f155376e4",
      "headRepository": "afrind/draft-frindell-moq-timestamp",
      "headRefName": "origin-on-posix-clock",
      "headRefOid": "b0e308f80d167a63c70e8c02a4065b68b3948d98",
      "closedAt": "2026-10-31T12:55:28Z",
      "mergedAt": "2026-10-31T12:55:28Z",
      "mergedBy": "afrind",
